// lexdb over TDS: the third bug slice (design/lexdb-robust.md, "The third bug slice"), checked against SQL Server 2022 (generated by
// tests/lexdb/gen_mssql.py bugs3 from mssql_bugs3_queries.txt): MIN and MAX of equal instants with different offsets keep the first one read (GROUP
// BY, a window, a heap, NULLs, no rows); SWITCHOFFSET, TODATETIMEOFFSET, AT TIME ZONE, MIN and MAX keep their argument's scale; SELECT ... INTO
// counts its rows; FORMAT's C has no decimals for the yen, the won, the rupiah and the Colombian peso; a CHECK's text in INFORMATION_SCHEMA.
// CHECK_CONSTRAINTS and sys.check_constraints as SQL Server writes it. Each batch runs with SET lexdb_batch off and on; each expect line: "same: "
// and the batch's result sets and counts, or its error number.
// expect: ok
// expect: (7)
// expect: ok
